He's probably just embarrassed.

990
00:43:00.036 --> 00:43:02.198
This is gonna be
a game changer, trust me.

991
00:43:02.580 --> 00:43:03.570
[Sharon groans]

992
00:43:03.873 --> 00:43:05.114
You need some help?

993
00:43:05.208 --> 00:43:06.870
[Sharon] I need the Jaws of Life.

994
00:43:09.170 --> 00:43:10.581
[laughs]

995
00:43:10.671 --> 00:43:13.209
Um, I don't think
you have that on quite right,

996
00:43:13.299 --> 00:43:14.460
but it's gonna look amazing.

997
00:43:14.550 --> 00:43:16.963
I look like a Lane Bryant mannequin.

998
00:43:17.720 --> 00:43:20.838
I'm sorry, I'm just trying
to picture your serial killer

999
00:43:20.932 --> 00:43:22.639
trying to peel you out of that thing.

1000
00:43:22.725 --> 00:43:24.967
- He's gonna have to use his teeth.
- If he has teeth.

1001
00:43:26.145 --> 00:43:27.477
When you guys are finished joking,

1002
00:43:27.563 --> 00:43:28.895
can you get me some scissors?

1003
00:43:28.981 --> 00:43:30.563
I can't feel my feet.

1004
00:43:38.574 --> 00:43:39.781
[Chris] Is that the one
I showed you?

1005
00:43:39.867 --> 00:43:41.324
No. Found it on Zillow.

1006
00:43:41.410 --> 00:43:43.026
Check it out.

1007
00:43:43.121 --> 00:43:45.033
- This has a media room.
- Oh, sick.

1008
00:43:45.123 --> 00:43:46.489
You don't need a media room,

1009
00:43:46.582 --> 00:43:48.995
you need your son to live
in a good school district.

1010
00:43:49.085 --> 00:43:51.122
Mom. You shouldn't be adding salt.

1011
00:43:51.212 --> 00:43:53.795
It's spaghetti. I always
add salt to my spaghetti.

1012
00:43:53.881 --> 00:43:56.589
Mom, did you not get the article
I sent you on blood pressure?

1013
00:43:57.635 --> 00:43:59.672
[cell phone ringing]

1014
00:44:01.055 --> 00:44:04.048
Oh, shoot. Could... Could you
excuse me for just a sec?

1015
00:44:07.854 --> 00:44:10.597
Don't say "sick". You're 40 years old.

1016
00:44:11.232 --> 00:44:12.848
[Diane] Hi, how are you?

1017
00:44:13.693 --> 00:44:16.231
Come visit you? That's crazy!

1018
00:44:19.657 --> 00:44:22.946
What? Well, I don't know
how I can do that, you know?

1019
00:44:23.828 --> 00:44:25.114
Yeah?

1020
00:44:25.997 --> 00:44:28.614
Oh. Well, okay.

1021
00:44:28.708 --> 00:44:30.244
I'm just gonna have
to come up with a reason.

1022
00:44:30.334 --> 00:44:33.077
- [Jill] Mom?
- Uh-oh. I got to go.

1023
00:44:33.171 --> 00:44:35.504
Okay, yes, and I will. Okay, bye.

1024
00:44:36.048 --> 00:44:38.882
- [Adrianne] Is everything okay?
- [sighs] No. No.

1025
00:44:39.844 --> 00:44:42.587
That was my neighbor. And, um...

1026
00:44:42.680 --> 00:44:44.888
There was a robber,
or a burglar, I don't know.

1027
00:44:44.974 --> 00:44:47.637
Anyway, they think
that the house was burgled!

1028
00:44:47.727 --> 00:44:49.764
- Burgled?
- It's shocking!

1029
00:44:50.521 --> 00:44:53.810
But you know something? I think
I need to get back there ASAP to help.

1030
00:44:53.900 --> 00:44:55.607
What do you mean, help?

1031
00:44:55.693 --> 00:44:58.060
What I mean is the authorities...
they may want to ask some questions.

1032
00:44:58.154 --> 00:45:00.771
So I do need to get back there now.

1033
00:45:01.073 --> 00:45:02.063
The authorities?

1034
00:45:02.158 --> 00:45:04.400
I'm not a suspect. I'm not suspicious.

1035
00:45:04.493 --> 00:45:06.655
It's not that kind of thing.
But I'm so worried.

1036
00:45:06.746 --> 00:45:09.363
This world is just not
a safe place for you anymore.

1037
00:45:09.457 --> 00:45:11.164
I'm sorry, and...

1038
00:45:11.250 --> 00:45:14.084
I'm really gonna try
to keep that in my mind, okay?

1039
00:45:14.337 --> 00:45:17.000
But anyway, I need to book
a flight back tomorrow.

1040
00:45:17.089 --> 00:45:19.752
Do I just not turn you on anymore?

1041
00:45:19.842 --> 00:45:23.176
I mean, I get it after 35 years
and three kids, but am I...

1042
00:45:23.262 --> 00:45:26.096
Is it just not exciting anymore?

1043
00:45:26.182 --> 00:45:27.423
I love you, Carol.

1044
00:45:27.516 --> 00:45:29.803
I know you love me,
and I love you.

1045
00:45:30.061 --> 00:45:31.677
Then what is the problem?

1046
00:45:31.771 --> 00:45:34.809
The problem is we haven't
even tried to make love

1047
00:45:34.899 --> 00:45:36.390
since your retirement party.

1048
00:45:36.484 --> 00:45:38.316
And we both know
how that turned out.

1049
00:45:38.402 --> 00:45:40.735
You yourself said
there was something wrong

1050
00:45:40.821 --> 00:45:42.232
with the lamb that night.

1051
00:45:42.490 --> 00:45:45.073
We both know there was
nothing wrong with the lamb.

1052
00:45:45.159 --> 00:45:46.445
I'm the one who made it.

1053
00:45:46.535 --> 00:45:48.618
I'm not having this conversation.

1054
00:45:48.704 --> 00:45:52.038
[sighs] Bruce, Vivian said
that it is so normal for men...

1055
00:45:52.124 --> 00:45:53.660
Wait. Vivian?

1056
00:45:53.751 --> 00:45:55.959
Dr. Schaefer said there are
safe and effective ways...

1057
00:45:56.045 --> 00:45:57.502
You talked to Dr. Schaefer?

1058
00:45:57.588 --> 00:46:00.046
I did not think
you'd want to talk to him.

1059
00:46:00.132 --> 00:46:03.045
- I don't want to talk to him!
- See? I knew that! I knew that!

1060
00:46:03.135 --> 00:46:05.468
He asked me,
"Does he still pleasure himself?"

1061
00:46:05.554 --> 00:46:07.796
- Oh, my God!
- And I said, "I have no idea!"

1062
00:46:08.349 --> 00:46:10.807
Carol! This is enough!

1063
00:46:10.893 --> 00:46:13.180
[shouts] Bruce! I want to have sex!

1064
00:46:13.271 --> 00:46:14.557
[dog whines]

1065
00:46:15.273 --> 00:46:16.730
Hello.

1066
00:46:19.735 --> 00:46:20.896
[huffs]

1067
00:46:20.987 --> 00:46:22.228
Excuse me.

1068
00:46:23.239 --> 00:46:24.480
[both sigh]

1069
00:46:24.573 --> 00:46:27.657
Okay, come on, baby.
Get your leg up there.

1070
00:46:27.743 --> 00:46:28.859
[grunts]

1071
00:46:29.287 --> 00:46:30.573
Goddang it.

1072
00:46:30.663 --> 00:46:31.653
[engine fails]

1073
00:46:31.747 --> 00:46:32.783
Come on.

1074
00:46:33.165 --> 00:46:35.703
What, you can't
get it turned on, huh?

1075
00:46:52.268 --> 00:46:54.351
Hi. Do you have a reservation?

1076
00:46:54.437 --> 00:46:56.349
No, actually I'm meeting someone.

1077
00:46:56.439 --> 00:46:58.146
His name is George.

1078
00:46:58.232 --> 00:46:59.814
He's a tax accountant.

1079
00:47:01.152 --> 00:47:03.064
Right. Follow me.

1080
00:47:05.906 --> 00:47:07.647
Enjoy your meal.

1081
00:47:07.742 --> 00:47:09.404
Hey, you have arms!

1082
00:47:09.952 --> 00:47:11.864
It would've been fine
if you didn't, but it's...

1083
00:47:11.954 --> 00:47:13.320
better that you do. Hey.

1084
00:47:13.414 --> 00:47:16.953
So nice to... Whoa, whoa, whoa.
I'll take care of it.

1085
00:47:17.043 --> 00:47:19.410
This is why I don't leave the house.

1086
00:47:22.048 --> 00:47:25.712
- Shall we start again?
- I'm afraid to reenter.

1087
00:47:25.801 --> 00:47:27.167
Nah.

1088
00:47:27.261 --> 00:47:29.844
We can take it right from here.

1089
00:47:30.306 --> 00:47:31.422
[Sharon] Okay.

1090
00:47:32.933 --> 00:47:34.469
So, what about you?

1091
00:47:35.311 --> 00:47:37.724
- You work?
- Um, yes.

1092
00:47:37.813 --> 00:47:40.521
Actually, I'm currently working
on my drinking. [chuckles]

1093
00:47:40.608 --> 00:47:42.065
[both laugh]

1094
00:47:42.443 --> 00:47:44.184
You have a nice laugh.

1095
00:47:46.197 --> 00:47:47.483
Thank you.

1096
00:47:48.032 --> 00:47:49.989
Actually, I'm a federal judge.

1097
00:47:50.451 --> 00:47:51.737
Wow.

1098
00:47:52.787 --> 00:47:54.494
- Really?
- Yeah.

1099
00:47:55.539 --> 00:47:59.283
And I do have the power
to put you in handcuffs.

1100
00:47:59.377 --> 00:48:01.585
I don't know
why I said that. Really.

1101
00:48:01.670 --> 00:48:03.457
I'm sorry. I...

1102
00:48:04.006 --> 00:48:06.840
I was guessing what you might be
thinking and...

1103
00:48:06.926 --> 00:48:09.418
I mean, not you, but men.

1104
00:48:09.512 --> 00:48:12.846
Not like all men
think the same, but...

1105
00:48:13.682 --> 00:48:16.140
I'm sorry I'm not better at this,
but this is...

1106
00:48:16.227 --> 00:48:17.343
Whoa.

1107
00:48:18.229 --> 00:48:19.561
Can I make a confession?

1108
00:48:20.022 --> 00:48:22.935
Uh, I changed
my shirt today six times

1109
00:48:23.025 --> 00:48:24.687
and I only have five shirts.

1110
00:48:25.653 --> 00:48:28.316
And the irony is
that they're all exactly alike.

1111
00:48:28.656 --> 00:48:30.648
Blue, button-down, Brooks Brothers.

1112
00:48:30.741 --> 00:48:32.858
Well, who doesn't love Brooks Brothers?

1113
00:48:32.952 --> 00:48:34.488
Not this guy.

1114
00:48:35.246 --> 00:48:37.112
When did dating get so complicated?

1115
00:48:37.206 --> 00:48:39.869
I mean, it used to be
you'd go to a dance

1116
00:48:39.959 --> 00:48:43.202
and bada-boom bada-bing,
you'd get married and pregnant.

1117
00:48:43.295 --> 00:48:45.457
Now you have to come up with

1118
00:48:45.548 --> 00:48:47.915
earth-shattering theories on life

1119
00:48:48.008 --> 00:48:51.718
before you even get a "wink."
What is that, a "wink" online?

1120
00:48:51.804 --> 00:48:55.969
You know, you are so much better
at this than you think you are.

1121
00:48:58.018 --> 00:48:59.429
Thank you.

1122
00:48:59.520 --> 00:49:01.227
You are too, for the record.

1123
00:49:02.064 --> 00:49:05.228
All my past relationships
taught me one thing.

1124
00:49:06.694 --> 00:49:08.356
I can't sleep with men.

1125
00:49:08.446 --> 00:49:11.314
Well, now, there's a revelation
I was not expecting.

1126
00:49:11.407 --> 00:49:14.400
No, but sex is fine.
I just can't sleep.

1127
00:49:15.453 --> 00:49:17.319
Okay, that makes more sense.

1128
00:49:17.413 --> 00:49:19.996
Now I can focus on
what you're gonna say next.

1129
00:49:20.082 --> 00:49:22.870
I can't understand
how men can sleep anywhere.

1130
00:49:22.960 --> 00:49:25.043
On the floor, in a bed, on a couch.

1131
00:49:25.129 --> 00:49:27.291
I'm staring at the ceiling
and they're off

1132
00:49:27.381 --> 00:49:29.418
in some blissful dreamscape.

1133
00:49:30.468 --> 00:49:34.553
Well, they say that bad sleep
is a sign of a bad relationship.

1134
00:49:34.638 --> 00:49:36.971
Yeah, well, I can attest to that.

1135
00:49:38.350 --> 00:49:40.216
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1136
00:49:40.311 --> 00:49:41.597
Wow.

1137
00:49:42.688 --> 00:49:44.975
I never thought
I'd be back here again.

1138
00:49:45.399 --> 00:49:46.435
Me, neither.

1139
00:49:47.443 --> 00:49:48.479
Here we go.

1140
00:49:50.779 --> 00:49:51.769
[moans appreciatively]

1141
00:49:52.907 --> 00:49:56.491
- Is it as good as you remember?
- Maybe better.

1142
00:50:00.664 --> 00:50:02.121
Let me ask you a question.

1143
00:50:02.833 --> 00:50:05.120
What's your favorite thing
in the whole world?

1144
00:50:06.378 --> 00:50:08.119
Well, that's a very broad question.

1145
00:50:08.214 --> 00:50:09.330
Um...

1146
00:50:11.175 --> 00:50:12.507
Arm tickles.

1147
00:50:12.593 --> 00:50:15.006
- Come on.
- No, without a doubt.

1148
00:50:15.638 --> 00:50:18.506
No, it's true.
I'm a girl of simple pleasures.

1149
00:50:18.599 --> 00:50:21.433
[laughs] Says the girl
with a staff of 150!

1150
00:50:21.519 --> 00:50:23.226
Ah, but it would be so much better

1151
00:50:23.312 --> 00:50:25.304
if they were all tickling my arms.

1152
00:50:30.402 --> 00:50:33.440
You know what I love to do
that I never do anymore?

1153
00:50:34.073 --> 00:50:38.864
Listen to a full album on vinyl
from beginning to end.

1154
00:50:40.579 --> 00:50:43.447
Vinyl sure has made
a comeback, hasn't it?

1155
00:50:43.832 --> 00:50:46.324
Well, some things
stand the test of time.

1156
00:50:49.880 --> 00:50:50.996
That they do.

1157
00:50:56.762 --> 00:50:59.721
[romantic music playing]

1158
00:51:18.075 --> 00:51:19.532
[music stops]

1159
00:51:19.618 --> 00:51:20.779
[instructor claps]

1160
00:51:20.869 --> 00:51:22.986
Dance is about connection.

1161
00:51:23.247 --> 00:51:25.364
It can't just be routine.

1162
00:51:25.457 --> 00:51:28.245
Moving in unison
is not the same as dancing.

1163
00:51:30.129 --> 00:51:31.165
Right.

1164
00:51:32.798 --> 00:51:34.039
[sighs]

1165
00:51:34.425 --> 00:51:36.041
[Carol] I think
we're done for the night.

1166
00:51:37.177 --> 00:51:38.213
Sorry.

1167
00:51:49.857 --> 00:51:53.601
I was 14. She was 17.
She could drive a car.

1168
00:51:54.153 --> 00:51:57.021
And she was sitting behind the wheel.

1169
00:51:57.114 --> 00:51:58.946
She said, "Come here."

1170
00:52:01.368 --> 00:52:02.904
This is me.

1171
00:52:03.996 --> 00:52:05.737
Thank you for making tonight so easy.

1172
00:52:05.831 --> 00:52:08.824
Oh... It was a great, great pleasure.

1173
00:52:14.882 --> 00:52:16.965
Um, I have to ask you this.

1174
00:52:17.051 --> 00:52:18.917
First of all, I think you're great.

1175
00:52:19.011 --> 00:52:22.049
And second,
I know that the chances of this

1176
00:52:22.139 --> 00:52:25.428
going past this evening are slim, but...

1177
00:52:26.310 --> 00:52:28.017
would you mind if I...

1178
00:52:28.604 --> 00:52:29.936
kissed you?

1179
00:52:30.022 --> 00:52:31.308
If I had a nickel

1180
00:52:31.398 --> 00:52:33.355
for every time
someone asked me that.

1181
00:52:33.442 --> 00:52:36.276
All right, all right. I'll just rewind
the tape about 30 seconds.

1182
00:52:36.362 --> 00:52:38.103
Shut up and kiss me.

1183
00:52:40.199 --> 00:52:41.440
Oh, hell.

1184
00:52:54.505 --> 00:52:55.791
[clears throat]

1185
00:52:57.091 --> 00:52:59.583
I think this belongs to you.

1186
00:53:05.099 --> 00:53:06.510
Thank you.

1187
00:53:08.727 --> 00:53:10.684
[Sharon] Ginsburger!

1188
00:53:24.118 --> 00:53:26.701
Ooh. I'm gonna need
a bigger back seat.

1189
00:53:28.872 --> 00:53:32.491
Paging Dr. Derek.

1190
00:53:37.047 --> 00:53:38.458
- [Adrianne] Is this good?
- Uh-huh.

1191
00:53:38.549 --> 00:53:40.381
This is fine, this is totally fine.

1192
00:53:40.467 --> 00:53:41.878
Okay.

1193
00:53:44.304 --> 00:53:46.842
I love how your generation
still feels the need

1194
00:53:46.932 --> 00:53:48.514
to get fancy for air travel.

1195
00:53:48.600 --> 00:53:49.932
It's so cute.

1196
00:53:51.437 --> 00:53:52.678
[Diane] Okay...

1197
00:53:52.771 --> 00:53:55.013
- Call me when you get back to L.A.
- Of course.

1198
00:53:55.107 --> 00:53:56.564
- I love you.
- I love you, too.

1199
00:53:56.650 --> 00:53:58.107
- Be safe.
- Bye-bye.

1200
00:53:58.193 --> 00:53:59.900
- Love you.
- Love you!

1201
00:54:00.738 --> 00:54:02.195
[groans]

1202
00:54:09.079 --> 00:54:10.445
[groans]

1203
00:54:13.625 --> 00:54:15.366
Quite an escape, Houdini.

1204
00:54:16.336 --> 00:54:19.295
Oh, God. I can't believe I'm doing this.

1205
00:54:19.381 --> 00:54:21.623
[pop music playing]

1206
00:54:28.348 --> 00:54:30.715
[inaudible]

1207
00:54:44.865 --> 00:54:46.481
[inaudible]

1208
00:54:48.494 --> 00:54:49.780
You know, I can't get over it.

1209
00:54:49.870 --> 00:54:53.238
Honestly, I'm not sure
I've ever seen a prettier sky.

1210
00:54:53.332 --> 00:54:55.745
- Mmm.
- Right?

1211
00:54:55.834 --> 00:54:57.871
- Cheers.
- Oh, cheers, okay.

1212
00:54:57.961 --> 00:54:59.168
Boom.

1213
00:54:59.505 --> 00:55:00.962
Can I show you something?

1214
00:55:01.757 --> 00:55:03.498
- Sure.
- Come with me.

1215
00:55:03.592 --> 00:55:04.582
What are we doing? Wait.

1216
00:55:04.676 --> 00:55:06.838
- Are you nervous?
- Oh... Should I be?

1217
00:55:06.929 --> 00:55:08.090
Mm-hmm.

1218
00:55:08.180 --> 00:55:09.842
I'm not sure I've ever met anybody

1219
00:55:09.932 --> 00:55:12.595
who owned their own barn before.

1220
00:55:13.143 --> 00:55:15.100
You got to get out
of the city more often.

1221
00:55:15.187 --> 00:55:18.180
Uh-huh. Oh, no, wait, no.
Forget it.

1222
00:55:18.273 --> 00:55:20.936
There is no chance in hell
I'm getting into that thing.

1223
00:55:21.026 --> 00:55:22.267
No. No!

1224
00:55:22.361 --> 00:55:24.398
You're gonna love it.
It's gonna be great.

1225
00:55:24.488 --> 00:55:26.946
I'm sorry, but...
What are you talking about?

1226
00:55:27.032 --> 00:55:28.443
No, I'm not getting in there.

1227
00:55:28.534 --> 00:55:30.776
These are the controls.
Don't touch anything.

1228
00:55:30.869 --> 00:55:32.201
If you touch it, we'll crash.

1229
00:55:33.038 --> 00:55:34.904
- Don't say that.
- I'm kidding.

1230
00:55:34.998 --> 00:55:36.955
This is my baby, okay?

1231
00:55:37.042 --> 00:55:38.999
See that "B" there? You see?

1232
00:55:39.086 --> 00:55:42.705
- It's a Beechcraft Bonanza V-Tail.
- Okay.

1233
00:55:42.798 --> 00:55:45.415
And it's been my passion project
for the last...

1234
00:55:46.009 --> 00:55:47.170
20 years.

1235
00:55:47.261 --> 00:55:49.423
Twenty years! Wait a minute.
How old is this thing?

1236
00:55:49.513 --> 00:55:51.675
- It's a 1951.
- Whoa!

1237
00:55:51.765 --> 00:55:53.973
I'm a 1951! Let me out of here!

1238
00:55:54.059 --> 00:55:55.675
No, seriously.

1239
00:55:55.769 --> 00:55:57.977
- Okay, we're going up.
- Wait, no.

1240
00:55:58.063 --> 00:55:59.270
I'm gonna regret this!

1241
00:56:06.405 --> 00:56:09.944
Oh, please. No, no, you have
a death wish. Death wish!

1242
00:56:10.033 --> 00:56:12.400
- Please.
- We're all gonna die someday, Diane.

1243
00:56:12.786 --> 00:56:16.075
I just feel like it's worth living
a little bit while we still can.

1244
00:56:16.164 --> 00:56:17.700
[screams]

1245
00:56:17.791 --> 00:56:19.908
[pop music playing]

1246
00:56:28.510 --> 00:56:30.126
[inaudible]

1247
00:56:36.476 --> 00:56:38.308
Overwhelming, huh?

1248
00:56:38.395 --> 00:56:39.761
Wanna hold on to the...

1249
00:56:39.855 --> 00:56:42.313
- Oh, okay.
- Just hold on to it.

1250
00:56:42.399 --> 00:56:43.731
I'll hold on.

1251
00:56:48.113 --> 00:56:49.524
- No!
- See that?

1252
00:56:49.615 --> 00:56:50.651
Yes.

1253
00:56:55.287 --> 00:56:57.244
Oh, no, that's...

1254
00:57:01.501 --> 00:57:04.084
- I'm gonna bank, to the right.
- You're gonna bank?

1255
00:57:07.507 --> 00:57:08.998
[Diane] Oh...

1256
00:57:09.092 --> 00:57:10.549
[Mitchell] You know what that is?

1257
00:57:10.636 --> 00:57:13.049
Yes. That's Cathedral Rock.

1258
00:57:13.138 --> 00:57:14.595
That's right.

1259
00:57:15.390 --> 00:57:17.928
Oh, my God.

1260
00:57:38.830 --> 00:57:40.196
[sighs]

1261
00:57:49.716 --> 00:57:51.173
[whinnying]

1262
00:57:53.512 --> 00:57:55.128
And all this, though,
from being a pilot

1263
00:57:55.222 --> 00:57:57.965
- is what you're saying, right? This?
- No.

1264
00:57:58.058 --> 00:57:59.924
- No?
- No, what happened was

1265
00:58:00.018 --> 00:58:01.680
I got out of the Air Force,

1266
00:58:01.770 --> 00:58:05.229
and I went to work for this
aeronautical research lab.

1267
00:58:05.315 --> 00:58:08.558
And, you know, I came up
with this design that...

1268
00:58:09.069 --> 00:58:11.482
that reduced engine drag in a jet.

1269
00:58:11.571 --> 00:58:13.563
It's silly, but it's a big patent,

1270
00:58:13.657 --> 00:58:16.445
and this is what happened
right here. See?

1271
00:58:16.535 --> 00:58:18.151
[cell phone vibrating]

1272
00:58:20.539 --> 00:58:22.622
You're gonna have
to introduce me to your family.

1273
00:58:22.708 --> 00:58:23.994
When can I meet them?

1274
00:58:24.084 --> 00:58:26.292
- I don't think that's a good idea.
- Why?

1275
00:58:26.378 --> 00:58:29.371
Because they're still very sensitive
about their father and...

1276
00:58:30.632 --> 00:58:32.043
What about you?

1277
00:58:34.928 --> 00:58:37.170
Well, I'm... I mean, I loved him.

1278
00:58:38.890 --> 00:58:42.099
But I guess I realized
I was in mourning

1279
00:58:42.185 --> 00:58:43.972
for the end of something.

1280
00:58:44.062 --> 00:58:45.473
It's been a long time.

1281
00:58:45.939 --> 00:58:48.727
I mean, I guess, I don't know,
the world sees your...

1282
00:58:49.484 --> 00:58:50.941
your relationship in one way,

1283
00:58:51.028 --> 00:58:53.315
you just kind of go along, but...

1284
00:58:53.405 --> 00:58:55.146
then the truth is...

1285
00:58:56.658 --> 00:58:58.775
it had been over between us
for a long time.

1286
00:58:59.828 --> 00:59:00.944
So...

1287
00:59:01.705 --> 00:59:03.162
what do you think of that?

1288
00:59:04.458 --> 00:59:06.290
You don't want to hear
my sad story, do you?

1289
00:59:06.376 --> 00:59:07.992
Maybe you should tell me yours.

1290
00:59:08.086 --> 00:59:09.543
[Mitchell] I don't have a sad story.

1291
00:59:09.629 --> 00:59:12.121
[Diane] You don't have a sad story
'cause you're rich.

1292
00:59:12.215 --> 00:59:14.502
It's been 24 hours
and there's still no answer.

1293
00:59:14.593 --> 00:59:16.004
Okay, I'm sure she's fine.

1294
00:59:16.094 --> 00:59:17.505
You're so sure everything is fine!

1295
00:59:17.596 --> 00:59:19.337
She could be passed out
in a ditch somewhere!

1296
00:59:19.431 --> 00:59:21.844
Adrianne, please calm down.

1297
00:59:21.933 --> 00:59:24.550
- I'm calling Jill.
- You're being hormonal!

1298
00:59:25.479 --> 00:59:26.720
[vibrates]

1299
00:59:40.786 --> 00:59:42.277
[vibrates]

1300
00:59:47.542 --> 00:59:51.252
[pop music playing]

1301
01:00:01.515 --> 01:00:03.097
Sharon, is that you?

1302
01:00:04.684 --> 01:00:06.767
Tom? Hi.

1303
01:00:06.853 --> 01:00:08.344
Wow! Hi!

1304
01:00:08.438 --> 01:00:09.770
Hi...

1305
01:00:10.148 --> 01:00:12.231
- Unexpected.
- Yeah.

1306
01:00:16.738 --> 01:00:18.229
Your hair's... dark.

1307
01:00:18.323 --> 01:00:19.313
Oh, it's dyed.

1308
01:00:19.407 --> 01:00:21.945
- I know.
- Right, right.

1309
01:00:22.035 --> 01:00:23.526
I want to introduce you to someone.

1310
01:00:23.620 --> 01:00:24.952
Oh, actually, I have to...

1311
01:00:25.038 --> 01:00:26.574
[Tom] Babe! Come here.

1312
01:00:27.207 --> 01:00:29.790
Babe, babe,
I want you to meet Sharon.

1313
01:00:29.876 --> 01:00:31.913
Sharon, this is my fiancée, Cheryl.

1314
01:00:32.003 --> 01:00:34.541
It is so nice to meet you!

1315
01:00:34.631 --> 01:00:36.247
I've heard so much about you.

1316
01:00:36.341 --> 01:00:37.832
Sharon?

1317
01:00:37.926 --> 01:00:39.508
Excuse me, are you Sharon?

1318
01:00:39.594 --> 01:00:41.506
- Yeah.
- I'm so sorry I'm late.

1319
01:00:41.596 --> 01:00:44.760
I was in a complicated sinus surgery.

1320
01:00:44.850 --> 01:00:46.637
Don't ask. [chuckles]

1321
01:00:46.726 --> 01:00:48.592
Hi, I'm Dr. Derek.

1322
01:00:48.687 --> 01:00:50.178
You can just call me Derek.

1323
01:00:50.272 --> 01:00:51.388
Hi, I'm Tom.

1324
01:00:51.481 --> 01:00:53.939
- Kill me now.
- I'm sorry, who are you?

1325
01:00:54.025 --> 01:00:57.518
Dr. Derek. Derek. Sharon's date.

1326
01:00:57.612 --> 01:01:00.480
- Wow.
- Hi. I am Cheryl.

1327
01:01:01.032 --> 01:01:03.570
I didn't know you were seeing someone.
That's great.

1328
01:01:03.660 --> 01:01:06.653
You look so amazing
without your mask!

1329
01:01:07.831 --> 01:01:10.164
[coos] Oh, how sweet.

1330
01:01:10.625 --> 01:01:13.117
You should bring Dr. Derek
to the party next week.

1331
01:01:13.211 --> 01:01:15.203
- What?
- The double-engagement party.

1332
01:01:15.297 --> 01:01:16.333
Didn't Jared tell you?

1333
01:01:16.548 --> 01:01:17.755
[Tom] Cheryl and I got engaged.

1334
01:01:17.841 --> 01:01:20.208
We've having a little celebration
with our friends.

1335
01:01:20.302 --> 01:01:22.419
But it really is for Jared and Kate.

1336
01:01:22.512 --> 01:01:24.754
- [Cheryl] We would so love to have you.
- [Tom] Yes.

1337
01:01:24.848 --> 01:01:26.965
- And you, too, Doctor.
- [Tom] Yeah.

1338
01:01:27.058 --> 01:01:29.516
Well, that sounds so nice!

1339
01:01:29.603 --> 01:01:32.846
Say, do you need a DJ?
I do that on the side.

1340
01:01:32.939 --> 01:01:34.396
- Ooh!
- Ooh!

1341
01:01:34.482 --> 01:01:36.690
[Tom] Do you do the vinyl
or what do you do, CDs?

1342
01:01:37.235 --> 01:01:39.227
[chattering]

1343
01:01:57.380 --> 01:01:59.622
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

1344
01:01:59.716 --> 01:02:01.673
You sure you're okay in the bar?

1345
01:02:01.760 --> 01:02:04.252
Yeah. It's gonna be like
the good old days.

1346
01:02:06.014 --> 01:02:07.346
Cheers.

1347
01:02:31.414 --> 01:02:33.155
Ha! Am I ever.

1348
01:02:33.917 --> 01:02:36.580
Inner goddess doing
the merengue, my ass!

1349
01:02:39.256 --> 01:02:41.748
So is this where you take all the boys?

1350
01:02:42.050 --> 01:02:45.009
Only the ones I don't want
to be seen with at the bar.

1351
01:02:46.680 --> 01:02:48.967
Well, I'll choose
to take that as a compliment.

1352
01:02:50.809 --> 01:02:52.641
Restricted area, huh?

1353
01:02:52.727 --> 01:02:54.514
[Vivian] Owner's perks.

1354
01:02:58.108 --> 01:02:59.565
Look at this.

1355
01:03:00.277 --> 01:03:02.690
A single solitary chair.

1356
01:03:02.779 --> 01:03:04.190
It's all a girl needs.

1357
01:03:04.281 --> 01:03:06.773
It's like a queen's throne
atop her castle.

1358
01:03:07.784 --> 01:03:09.571
Look. Look at the view.

1359
01:03:09.995 --> 01:03:13.363
[Arthur] Yeah. Look at
all those twinkling lights.

1360
01:03:13.581 --> 01:03:15.743
All those lives being lived.

1361
01:03:17.877 --> 01:03:20.711
As the poem goes,
you took the road less traveled,

1362
01:03:20.797 --> 01:03:23.665
and it made... all the difference.

1363
01:03:24.676 --> 01:03:27.009
You know, that's not really
what that poem is about.

1364
01:03:28.430 --> 01:03:29.716
- Is that right?
- No.

1365
01:03:30.265 --> 01:03:31.676
It's, um...

1366
01:03:32.559 --> 01:03:36.394
It's about how we...
we tell the story of our lives,

1367
01:03:37.063 --> 01:03:40.556
so we feel heroic, brave...

1368
01:03:41.943 --> 01:03:43.684
but in fact, there's no difference

1369
01:03:43.778 --> 01:03:45.565
in the paths to begin with.

1370
01:03:47.115 --> 01:03:48.902
- No difference in the paths?
- Nope.

1371
01:03:51.786 --> 01:03:53.618
Fascinating poem.

1372
01:04:01.046 --> 01:04:02.457
Arthur, come here.

1373
01:04:02.964 --> 01:04:06.583
Look at this. You see that
building with the red lights?

1374
01:04:07.385 --> 01:04:09.468
- Is that our diner?
- Yeah.

1375
01:04:10.972 --> 01:04:14.056
I can't believe your hotel
overlooks our favorite place.

1376
01:04:20.774 --> 01:04:23.517
According to the airline,
your mother never boarded her flight.

1377
01:04:23.610 --> 01:04:25.852
- Oh, my God.
- You said not to worry about it!

1378
01:04:25.945 --> 01:04:27.982
- Okay, you can worry now.
- What?

1379
01:04:28.073 --> 01:04:29.234
However...

1380
01:04:29.657 --> 01:04:31.444
we did trace a signal
to her cell phone.

1381
01:04:31.534 --> 01:04:32.991
- What?
- Okay.

1382
01:04:33.078 --> 01:04:35.070
- What does that mean?
- We know where she is.

1383
01:04:35.163 --> 01:04:37.120
- She's been kidnapped?
- I did not say that.

1384
01:04:37.207 --> 01:04:38.664
- Is there a ransom?
- You know where she is?

1385
01:04:38.750 --> 01:04:40.537
In a case like this,
it's best to remain calm.

1386
01:04:40.627 --> 01:04:42.209
- Let's get a grip, folks.
- You know where she is?

1387
01:04:42.295 --> 01:04:44.207
If you had to guess,
what would you say?

1388
01:04:44.297 --> 01:04:46.004
I don't have to guess,
I actually know.

1389
01:04:46.091 --> 01:04:47.502
- Well, then take us there!
- Can I see the pad?

1390
01:04:47.592 --> 01:04:50.380
I can't believe
you put Viagra in my beer.

1391
01:04:50.470 --> 01:04:52.427
Well, it was an innocent mistake.

1392
01:04:52.514 --> 01:04:54.881
Oh, innocent. How is it innocent?
You poisoned me.

1393
01:04:54.974 --> 01:04:56.181
Hardly.

1394
01:04:56.267 --> 01:04:58.509
Do not use that word.

1395
01:04:58.603 --> 01:05:01.471
- I'm sorry. How does it feel?
- Hard!

1396
01:05:01.564 --> 01:05:03.430
I thought we weren't
gonna use that word.

1397
01:05:03.525 --> 01:05:05.141
I can, you can't.

1398
01:05:05.235 --> 01:05:07.227
- God, there are so many rules.
- Don't, Carol!

1399
01:05:07.320 --> 01:05:09.937
- [tires squealing]
- Jeez.

1400
01:05:10.031 --> 01:05:12.148
I'll tell you something,
I don't think it ought to go to waste.

1401
01:05:12.242 --> 01:05:14.609
- [Bruce] Seriously! Stop it.
- [Carol] Calm down.

1402
01:05:14.702 --> 01:05:16.864
[sirens blaring]

1403
01:05:16.955 --> 01:05:18.992
Really? I'm being pulled over.

1404
01:05:19.916 --> 01:05:22.203
Sir, I'm gonna need you
to step out of the vehicle.

1405
01:05:22.293 --> 01:05:24.330
I don't think that's
a good idea, Officer.

1406
01:05:24.421 --> 01:05:27.164
Out of the car now!

1407
01:05:27.257 --> 01:05:28.623
Okay, okay.

1408
01:05:29.384 --> 01:05:30.920
Gosh darn it.

1409
01:05:32.220 --> 01:05:33.461
Man.

1410
01:05:35.306 --> 01:05:39.550
Look, I'm sorry.
Uh, my wife put Viagra in my drink.

1411
01:05:39.644 --> 01:05:41.556
It's actually true.
It's my bad, I'm so sorry.

1412
01:05:41.646 --> 01:05:44.263
But you see, it's just he's been
having a little trouble

1413
01:05:44.357 --> 01:05:47.270
in that department,
and he was embarrassed.

1414
01:05:47.360 --> 01:05:49.568
And if there's one thing
I know about this man,

1415
01:05:49.654 --> 01:05:51.566
it's that he really hates
to be embarrassed.

1416
01:05:51.656 --> 01:05:52.737
Isn't that true, Pup?

1417
01:05:52.824 --> 01:05:54.235
Oh, I hate a lot of things right now.

1418
01:05:54.325 --> 01:05:56.112
That's not even in the top three.

1419
01:05:56.327 --> 01:05:58.444
Will this affect your ability to drive?

1420
01:05:58.997 --> 01:06:00.329
[Bruce] No, ma'am.
Mmm-mmm.

1421
01:06:01.207 --> 01:06:02.573
Okay.

1422
01:06:03.001 --> 01:06:04.617
- Enjoy your night.
- [Bruce] Okay.

1423
01:06:05.795 --> 01:06:06.831
You, too.

1424
01:06:06.921 --> 01:06:08.503
Thank you.

1425
01:06:15.763 --> 01:06:17.254
[Mitchell] I think I like you.

1426
01:06:17.348 --> 01:06:20.591
Well, I think that's probably
just the wine talking, right?

1427
01:06:21.102 --> 01:06:22.309
Wait.

1428
01:06:23.730 --> 01:06:26.438
You know what?
I think I'm in trouble here.

1429
01:06:26.858 --> 01:06:29.020
- Oh, I'm well past trouble.
- Yeah?

1430
01:06:29.110 --> 01:06:30.942
- [thump]
- What?

1431
01:06:31.029 --> 01:06:32.520
I think I heard something.

1432
01:06:32.614 --> 01:06:34.150
It's probably just
the wine talking, right?

1433
01:06:34.240 --> 01:06:35.481
[chuckling]

1434
01:06:35.575 --> 01:06:37.942
And how often does the wine
talk in your world?

1435
01:06:38.036 --> 01:06:41.074
- [gate opens]
- Oh, my God. Wait, who... who is that?

1436
01:06:41.915 --> 01:06:44.658
- Mom?
- [Mitchell] Oh, boy.

1437
01:06:44.751 --> 01:06:46.083
[Diane shrieks]

1438
01:06:46.169 --> 01:06:48.331
- Oh, my God.
- Oh, my God.

1439
01:06:48.421 --> 01:06:50.208
Oh, my God!

1440
01:06:50.298 --> 01:06:52.415
Oh, my God! Mom!

1441
01:06:52.509 --> 01:06:54.717
Honey, let me explain.

1442
01:06:54.802 --> 01:06:56.714
What the heck is happening here?

1443
01:06:56.804 --> 01:07:00.969
Hi. You must be, uh,
Adrianne and Jill.

1444
01:07:01.059 --> 01:07:02.345
I'm Mitchell.

1445
01:07:02.435 --> 01:07:03.471
- Chris.
- Stop it!

1446
01:07:03.561 --> 01:07:05.177
Mitchell, can you just...

1447
01:07:05.271 --> 01:07:06.307
[shrieks]

1448
01:07:06.397 --> 01:07:07.433
You okay?

1449
01:07:07.524 --> 01:07:10.892
- [Jill] Mom!
- No, please. No, I'm fine.

1450
01:07:10.985 --> 01:07:13.398
Just let me explain, okay?
I'll be right back.

1451
01:07:13.488 --> 01:07:15.024
Wait, where are you going?

1452
01:07:17.450 --> 01:07:21.319
She's okay. She's perfectly...
She was in good hands. Relax.

1453
01:07:21.412 --> 01:07:23.278
- You relax!
- [Mitchell] No, it's okay.

1454
01:07:23.373 --> 01:07:25.410
- You relax!
- We've had a long day. I'm sorry.

1455
01:07:25.500 --> 01:07:27.833
I was just trying to give us
a little jumpstart.

1456
01:07:27.919 --> 01:07:30.002
I thought maybe if we had
a really nice night

1457
01:07:30.088 --> 01:07:31.829
and things sort of
naturally progressed,

1458
01:07:31.923 --> 01:07:34.336
then maybe
we would both feel better.

1459
01:07:34.425 --> 01:07:36.792
Great plan! Congratulations
on the execution.

1460
01:07:36.886 --> 01:07:40.345
Sorry. I really was just
trying to help you, Bruce.

1461
01:07:40.431 --> 01:07:42.548
Help me?
By never once considering

1462
01:07:42.642 --> 01:07:44.759
that I might have an opinion!

1463
01:07:45.270 --> 01:07:47.853
No, it's not just tonight.
It's everything, Carol!

1464
01:07:47.939 --> 01:07:49.896
You've got me taking dance lessons.

1465
01:07:49.983 --> 01:07:54.353
Dance lessons for a talent show
that I never even signed up for!

1466
01:07:54.445 --> 01:07:57.108
You've been going to my
No Kid Hungry fundraiser

1467
01:07:57.198 --> 01:07:58.734
for the past 15 years.

1468
01:07:58.825 --> 01:08:00.316
You always show up for me.

1469
01:08:00.410 --> 01:08:02.151
That was for dinner.

1470
01:08:02.245 --> 01:08:03.986
Well, forgive me for trying to find ways

1471
01:08:04.080 --> 01:08:05.287
to keep us connected.

1472
01:08:05.373 --> 01:08:07.330
"Hey, Bruce, here's something
you're gonna hate to do

1473
01:08:07.417 --> 01:08:10.785
for the next two months,
but in the end it'll be okay

1474
01:08:10.878 --> 01:08:14.417
because there will be
an onstage public shaming!

1475
01:08:14.507 --> 01:08:16.590
So happy anniversary!"

1476
01:08:17.760 --> 01:08:19.626
What, what? Sorry, sorry.

1477
01:08:19.721 --> 01:08:21.508
Didn't hear you at all,
because my husband

1478
01:08:21.598 --> 01:08:23.760
gave me these wonderful earplugs,

1479
01:08:23.850 --> 01:08:26.263
so we wouldn't have to listen
to each other anymore.

1480
01:08:26.352 --> 01:08:28.093
Happy anniversary!

1481
01:08:28.980 --> 01:08:30.562
Hey, and by the way,

1482
01:08:30.648 --> 01:08:32.264
I got us the earplugs
so you wouldn't miss

1483
01:08:32.358 --> 01:08:33.724
any of your TV shows,

1484
01:08:33.818 --> 01:08:36.777
just because I happen
to love to fall asleep

1485
01:08:36.863 --> 01:08:38.604
next to my wife in our bed!

1486
01:08:39.741 --> 01:08:41.528
So forgive me!

1487
01:08:43.036 --> 01:08:44.117
[bang]

1488
01:08:44.412 --> 01:08:45.823
[groans]

1489
01:08:46.748 --> 01:08:47.864
[grunts angrily]

1490
01:08:51.252 --> 01:08:52.584
[groans]

1491
01:08:54.881 --> 01:08:56.463
Okay, what are you doing?
Come on.

1492
01:08:57.175 --> 01:08:58.291
Diane, I know this...

1493
01:08:58.384 --> 01:09:00.501
I know this is not the direction
we hoped for this evening.

1494
01:09:00.595 --> 01:09:05.010
This is... It's such a disaster!
Do you see what I mean?

1495
01:09:05.099 --> 01:09:07.762
You've got to admit it was kind of funny.
A cop showed up!

1496
01:09:07.852 --> 01:09:09.343
No, it wasn't kind of funny.

1497
01:09:09.437 --> 01:09:12.054
This whole thing
is just one giant mistake.

1498
01:09:12.148 --> 01:09:13.434
You don't believe that.

1499
01:09:13.524 --> 01:09:15.356
I get that it's embarrassing,
but who gives a shit?

1500
01:09:15.443 --> 01:09:17.275
No, you know what?
You don't get it, Mitchell.

1501
01:09:17.362 --> 01:09:19.274
You know why?
Because you don't have kids.

1502
01:09:19.697 --> 01:09:22.781
Kids? They're like adults, your kids.

1503
01:09:23.743 --> 01:09:24.984
You know,

1504
01:09:25.078 --> 01:09:26.740
you're out here on your ranch,

1505
01:09:26.829 --> 01:09:28.616
with no one to take care of but yourself.

1506
01:09:28.706 --> 01:09:31.619
Okay, that's fine for you,
but that's not the real world.

1507
01:09:31.959 --> 01:09:34.667
I have a family
and I have responsibilities.

1508
01:09:34.754 --> 01:09:37.963
- I'm sorry, but that's my world.
- I'm sure I don't understand

1509
01:09:38.049 --> 01:09:39.631
everything you're
going through right now.

1510
01:09:39.717 --> 01:09:41.629
That's right. You don't have a clue.

1511
01:09:41.719 --> 01:09:45.429
Listen to me. Look at me.
I know we just met.

1512
01:09:45.515 --> 01:09:48.053
But you can't spend your entire life
just going around

1513
01:09:48.142 --> 01:09:49.758
taking care of other people.

1514
01:09:49.852 --> 01:09:51.809
That's also not part of the real world.

1515
01:09:51.896 --> 01:09:53.307
Okay, hey!

1516
01:09:53.648 --> 01:09:55.230
- Diane.
- What? What?

1517
01:09:55.316 --> 01:09:57.182
I'm saying it's okay
to be happy, Diane.

1518
01:09:58.069 --> 01:10:00.482
Well, I'm really...
I'm sorry, but I have to go.

1519
01:10:33.730 --> 01:10:36.143
[rock music playing]

1520
01:11:09.682 --> 01:11:11.048
[music fades]

1521
01:11:24.363 --> 01:11:26.275
Bruce. Bruce, honey.

1522
01:11:26.783 --> 01:11:27.899
What?

1523
01:11:28.409 --> 01:11:32.073
I know I've been acting
a little crazy lately.

1524
01:11:32.163 --> 01:11:35.201
And obviously
I went overboard tonight.

1525
01:11:35.291 --> 01:11:36.623
Really?

1526
01:11:36.709 --> 01:11:38.371
My gosh, I hadn't noticed.

1527
01:11:40.046 --> 01:11:41.787
I am so sorry.

1528
01:11:44.258 --> 01:11:45.999
I embarrassed you...

1529
01:11:47.637 --> 01:11:49.970
and I made you feel
like you didn't matter.

1530
01:11:50.431 --> 01:11:52.388
I just don't know
what's been going on with you

1531
01:11:52.475 --> 01:11:55.434
for the last few months
and it scares me.

1532
01:11:56.103 --> 01:11:58.470
I know what I did was wrong, and...

1533
01:11:59.774 --> 01:12:01.140
I'm sorry.

1534
01:12:03.319 --> 01:12:04.855
[sighs]

1535
01:12:04.946 --> 01:12:06.403
I got spooked.

1536
01:12:06.489 --> 01:12:08.230
Spooked?

1537
01:12:08.324 --> 01:12:10.441
Yeah, at the...

1538
01:12:12.370 --> 01:12:13.656
retirement party.

1539
01:12:13.746 --> 01:12:14.987
You know, I saw...

1540
01:12:15.998 --> 01:12:18.832
40 years just... vanish.

1541
01:12:19.418 --> 01:12:22.707
And I didn't know
who I was anymore.

1542
01:12:23.673 --> 01:12:25.665
Well, what was I gonna do?

1543
01:12:26.175 --> 01:12:27.507
What can I do?

1544
01:12:28.052 --> 01:12:29.384
I got scared.

1545
01:12:30.555 --> 01:12:32.012
I am scared.

1546
01:12:33.307 --> 01:12:37.142
And I need a little time
to figure out who I am again.

1547
01:12:37.562 --> 01:12:38.973
[Carol] I hear you.

1548
01:12:39.063 --> 01:12:42.727
And I'm not gonna try
to fix everything on my own...

1549
01:12:44.235 --> 01:12:46.272
tempting though that may be.

1550
01:12:46.362 --> 01:12:49.025
And I'm not gonna make you do
a bunch of stuff

1551
01:12:49.115 --> 01:12:51.778
that you don't want to do,
like dancing at the fundraiser.

1552
01:12:51.868 --> 01:12:53.985
I know you never wanted to do that.

1553
01:12:54.078 --> 01:12:55.819
So forget it, okay?

1554
01:12:57.248 --> 01:12:58.614
I'm going to bed.

1555
01:13:06.757 --> 01:13:09.340
[Carol] <i>Whoa, ice cream
straight from the tub?</i>

1556
01:13:09.427 --> 01:13:13.262
Yeah, well, I ran into Tom
and his very happy fiancée.

1557
01:13:13.347 --> 01:13:14.713
Ah!

1558
01:13:14.807 --> 01:13:16.594
They're hosting
a double-engagement party

1559
01:13:16.684 --> 01:13:18.141
at their house.

1560
01:13:18.227 --> 01:13:20.719
Oh, did I mention he calls her "babe"?

1561
01:13:20.813 --> 01:13:23.021
Which is sort of perfect
since she's a child.

1562
01:13:23.107 --> 01:13:24.223
- Oh, no.
- Yeah.

1563
01:13:24.317 --> 01:13:25.478
What did I miss?

1564
01:13:25.568 --> 01:13:28.185
Well, Sharon is never dating again.

1565
01:13:28.279 --> 01:13:29.861
And we're all miserable.

1566
01:13:29.947 --> 01:13:31.404
So basically nothing has changed.

1567
01:13:31.490 --> 01:13:33.026
Yeah, well...

1568
01:13:33.367 --> 01:13:37.031
Whoa. Since when
do you eat ice cream?

1569
01:13:37.121 --> 01:13:38.703
[mumbles] Since now.

1570
01:13:38.789 --> 01:13:40.997
So I take it things
went south for you, too?

1571
01:13:41.292 --> 01:13:42.999
I slept with Arthur.

1572
01:13:43.085 --> 01:13:44.872
Now, there's a shocker.

1573
01:13:44.962 --> 01:13:46.544
No, not sex.

1574
01:13:47.298 --> 01:13:49.961
I actually fell asleep with him.

1575
01:13:50.051 --> 01:13:52.839
You've never been able
to sleep with a man before!

1576
01:13:52.929 --> 01:13:54.295
I know.

1577
01:13:54.388 --> 01:13:57.005
So, I mean...
you didn't have sex?

1578
01:13:57.099 --> 01:13:59.512
We slept on a couch
and he tickled my arm.

1579
01:13:59.602 --> 01:14:03.312
Oh, boy, now this is a disaster.
When is he leaving?

1580
01:14:03.397 --> 01:14:05.935
Not soon enough!
God, I got a brain freeze.

1581
01:14:06.400 --> 01:14:07.732
Here, give that to a professional.

1582
01:14:07.818 --> 01:14:09.275
Oh, my God!

1583
01:14:09.362 --> 01:14:11.649
Well, anyway,
I have an announcement.

1584
01:14:12.573 --> 01:14:13.563
Okay.

1585
01:14:13.658 --> 01:14:14.774
I am...

1586
01:14:14.867 --> 01:14:17.701
I'm officially... moving to Arizona.

1587
01:14:17.787 --> 01:14:20.404
- What?
- Oh, tell me it's for the pilot!

1588
01:14:20.498 --> 01:14:23.206
No, no, no.
For my daughters.

1589
01:14:23.960 --> 01:14:25.872
This has gone from bad to worse!

1590
01:14:25.962 --> 01:14:29.251
Well, I mean, they renovated
the basement for me,

1591
01:14:29.340 --> 01:14:31.002
and everything is slip resistant,

1592
01:14:31.092 --> 01:14:33.300
and I can walk into the tub.

1593
01:14:33.386 --> 01:14:34.922
- Oh, my God.
- Ick.

1594
01:14:35.012 --> 01:14:36.628
But what about the pilot?

1595
01:14:36.722 --> 01:14:39.556
Crashed and burned.
I mean, we're not 18 anymore.

1596
01:14:39.642 --> 01:14:41.099
Nope.

1597
01:14:41.185 --> 01:14:43.097
We're sure not spring flowers.

1598
01:14:43.187 --> 01:14:45.679
No. More like potpourri.

1599
01:14:45.773 --> 01:14:47.480
So, this is...

1600
01:14:47.566 --> 01:14:49.728
[groans] Oh, my God,
this is my last book club!

1601
01:14:49.819 --> 01:14:51.560
Oh, no, you're kidding!

1602
01:14:51.654 --> 01:14:52.861
Oh, Diane!

1603
01:14:52.947 --> 01:14:55.109
Do we even want to talk
about the book?

1604
01:14:55.199 --> 01:14:56.280
[groans]

1605
01:14:56.742 --> 01:14:59.029
- I hate this book, okay? Done.
- [Vivian] Me, too.

1606
01:14:59.120 --> 01:15:00.201
Yeah.

1607
01:15:00.287 --> 01:15:01.698
Are we really this pathetic?

1608
01:15:01.789 --> 01:15:04.406
None of us have
anything interesting to say?

1609
01:15:04.500 --> 01:15:08.540
Well, my little affair
ended with me in a pool

1610
01:15:08.629 --> 01:15:10.837
on top of an inflatable swan

1611
01:15:10.923 --> 01:15:13.131
and my daughters showing up
with the police!

1612
01:15:13.217 --> 01:15:16.551
Well, that certainly
qualifies as interesting.

1613
01:15:16.846 --> 01:15:19.759
I'm assuming
you were not in that pool alone.

1614
01:15:19.849 --> 01:15:21.431
Well... I was not.

1615
01:15:22.059 --> 01:15:23.470
Good for you.

1616
01:15:23.853 --> 01:15:26.391
Do I want to get us
another one of these?

1617
01:15:26.480 --> 01:15:28.267
- Oh, yeah.
- Yes!

1618
01:15:28.357 --> 01:15:29.848
[Diane] The sooner the better.

1619
01:15:31.819 --> 01:15:34.687
[pop music playing]

1620
01:15:53.132 --> 01:15:54.794
Men make life impossible.

1621
01:15:54.884 --> 01:15:56.546
Oh, God, tell me about it.

1622
01:15:56.635 --> 01:15:58.342
Well, you're one to talk.

1623
01:15:58.429 --> 01:16:02.013
Ditching God's gift to women
so you can live in a basement

1624
01:16:02.099 --> 01:16:04.887
and breastfeed
your daughter's children?

1625
01:16:04.977 --> 01:16:07.720
You know something?
That's really rich coming from you.

1626
01:16:07.813 --> 01:16:10.351
You've been stuck on Tom
for 18 years,

1627
01:16:10.441 --> 01:16:12.307
and you don't even like the guy.

1628
01:16:12.401 --> 01:16:13.812
He's not at your level.

1629
01:16:13.903 --> 01:16:16.771
Eighteen years ago,
you couldn't wait to get rid of him.

1630
01:16:16.864 --> 01:16:20.483
But you've conveniently erased
that little piece of history.

1631
01:16:20.743 --> 01:16:23.861
Wish I could erase
a little piece of my history.

1632
01:16:23.954 --> 01:16:25.115
[Diane sighs]

1633
01:16:25.206 --> 01:16:26.742
- Well...
- What?

1634
01:16:26.832 --> 01:16:28.824
I was fine until Arthur came along.

1635
01:16:28.918 --> 01:16:30.454
I had a happy existence.

1636
01:16:30.544 --> 01:16:32.001
Had a roster of men

1637
01:16:32.088 --> 01:16:34.250
that would satisfy my every whim.

1638
01:16:34.340 --> 01:16:37.879
Oh, my God,
I can't listen to this anymore.

1639
01:16:37.968 --> 01:16:40.961
You really believe you're satisfied?
How could you be?

1640
01:16:41.055 --> 01:16:42.887
You're so terrified of getting hurt

1641
01:16:42.973 --> 01:16:46.182
that you do everything you can
to push away love.

1642
01:16:46.268 --> 01:16:47.930
[sighs]

1643
01:16:48.896 --> 01:16:52.139
I'm gonna go back
to having sex and not caring.

1644
01:16:52.233 --> 01:16:54.020
Because that's what
works for me, okay?

1645
01:16:54.110 --> 01:16:56.352
Stop lying to yourself, Vivian.

1646
01:16:56.445 --> 01:16:58.778
Not everything in the world
is about sex.

1647
01:16:58.864 --> 01:17:00.651
Did you even read the book?

1648
01:17:00.950 --> 01:17:02.737
This is a love story.

1649
01:17:02.827 --> 01:17:05.786
That is what the world wants.
That's what the world needs.

1650
01:17:05.871 --> 01:17:08.989
So, okay, you can have sex
with anybody.

1651
01:17:09.083 --> 01:17:10.790
Well, whoop-de-fricking-do.

1652
01:17:10.876 --> 01:17:12.868
But you know what?
Eventually, people need

1653
01:17:12.962 --> 01:17:14.794
a little bit more than that.

1654
01:17:14.880 --> 01:17:19.545
Everybody's got baggage
and pain and problems, but...

1655
01:17:20.344 --> 01:17:22.882
even Christian Grey fell in love.

1656
01:17:22.972 --> 01:17:26.181
Yeah, and he was
fifty shades of fucked-up.

1657
01:17:26.267 --> 01:17:27.474
So...

1658
01:17:28.561 --> 01:17:29.802
here you go.

1659
01:17:29.895 --> 01:17:33.514
Book three? I am not sure
we'll survive another one.

1660
01:17:33.607 --> 01:17:35.690
Oh... Oh, God.

1661
01:17:39.280 --> 01:17:40.566
God, I...

1662
01:17:41.115 --> 01:17:44.608
I really am gonna miss this. Right?

1663
01:17:44.702 --> 01:17:46.614
[Vivian] Oh, honey.

1664
01:17:57.715 --> 01:17:59.456
- Have a good drive.
- Thanks again.

1665
01:18:01.552 --> 01:18:02.838
[sighs]

1666
01:18:08.184 --> 01:18:09.300
Ginsburg.

1667
01:18:10.769 --> 01:18:12.726
What's happening here?

1668
01:18:12.813 --> 01:18:16.022
[coos] Huh, honey?
What's happening?

1669
01:18:31.916 --> 01:18:34.579
[Diane] Look at you.
Look at you.

1670
01:18:34.668 --> 01:18:36.876
Yeah, yeah. Look at you.

1671
01:18:48.766 --> 01:18:50.803
[cell phone ringing]

1672
01:18:53.312 --> 01:18:54.553
[ringing stops]

1673
01:18:57.233 --> 01:18:58.519
[door closes]

1674
01:19:02.947 --> 01:19:04.404
You're not taking my calls.

1675
01:19:04.949 --> 01:19:07.032
I don't have my phone with me.

1676
01:19:07.368 --> 01:19:09.826
[cell phone ringing]

1677
01:19:09.912 --> 01:19:11.403
[ringing stops]

1678
01:19:13.916 --> 01:19:16.158
Do you know why
I first started on radio?

1679
01:19:16.877 --> 01:19:18.084
No, I don't.

1680
01:19:18.170 --> 01:19:20.082
Because I loved the idea

1681
01:19:20.172 --> 01:19:23.381
of no matter what I said
or what music I played...

1682
01:19:24.510 --> 01:19:26.092
millions of people could just

1683
01:19:26.178 --> 01:19:28.044
turn on their radios and hear it.

1684
01:19:32.017 --> 01:19:33.883
But then as I got older...

1685
01:19:34.353 --> 01:19:36.140
I realized that...

1686
01:19:37.481 --> 01:19:39.188
reaching millions and millions

1687
01:19:39.275 --> 01:19:40.891
of anonymous people...

1688
01:19:41.694 --> 01:19:43.686
doesn't come close...

1689
01:19:44.071 --> 01:19:47.155
to reaching
just one person you love.

1690
01:19:51.578 --> 01:19:54.321
And I'm... I'm leaving tomorrow.

1691
01:19:56.709 --> 01:19:58.450
And it got me thinking...

1692
01:20:00.379 --> 01:20:02.245
wouldn't it be nice if...

1693
01:20:02.339 --> 01:20:04.547
you were coming with me
to New York?

1694
01:20:05.843 --> 01:20:08.756
But then I thought about it
and I thought about you...

1695
01:20:10.014 --> 01:20:12.427
and your hotel and your rooftop...

1696
01:20:13.892 --> 01:20:17.056
and your inability
to make proper wishes.

1697
01:20:19.148 --> 01:20:22.357
I have no interest
in trying to change you, Vivian.

1698
01:20:24.570 --> 01:20:26.152
I love who you are.

1699
01:20:27.364 --> 01:20:29.276
Rich and independent...

1700
01:20:30.367 --> 01:20:31.949
and a total pain in the ass.

1701
01:20:33.162 --> 01:20:35.779
That does sound like... like me.

1702
01:20:36.498 --> 01:20:39.707
And here we are,
staring at two paths.

1703
01:20:42.004 --> 01:20:43.620
And I know how I feel.

1704
01:20:45.257 --> 01:20:47.840
I know that you're the person
that I want to talk to.

1705
01:20:49.386 --> 01:20:51.673
You're the person I want to listen to.

1706
01:20:53.182 --> 01:20:56.471
You're the person I want
to splash in the fountain.

1707
01:20:59.563 --> 01:21:01.429
You're my person, Slim.

1708
01:21:08.739 --> 01:21:11.777
And I just wanted to know
what you thought about that.

1709
01:21:18.332 --> 01:21:21.916
It's... It's been really nice
seeing you again, Arthur.

1710
01:21:22.878 --> 01:21:24.961
I hope you have a safe trip home.

1711
01:21:32.888 --> 01:21:34.629
[sighs]

1712
01:21:36.183 --> 01:21:38.675
[laughter]

1713
01:21:38.769 --> 01:21:41.011
[chattering]

1714
01:21:43.816 --> 01:21:45.728
[calypso music playing]

1715
01:21:45.818 --> 01:21:47.309
- Hi.
- Hi.

1716
01:21:58.622 --> 01:22:02.241
Hi, everybody. I'd like to take
a second to say a few words.

1717
01:22:02.334 --> 01:22:05.327
As most of you know,
I'm Tom Meyers, Jared's dad.

1718
01:22:05.421 --> 01:22:07.413
On behalf of my fiancée,
Cheryl, and myself,

1719
01:22:07.506 --> 01:22:08.872
I want to thank you all for coming.

1720
01:22:08.966 --> 01:22:10.798
Kate, we're so excited to welcome you

1721
01:22:10.884 --> 01:22:12.466
and invite you into the family.

1722
01:22:12.845 --> 01:22:16.338
- Jared, we are so very happy for you.
- Thanks, Dad.

1723
01:22:16.432 --> 01:22:20.051
As Shakespeare said, "Love looks
not with the eyes but with the mind."

1724
01:22:20.352 --> 01:22:22.014
How right he was.

1725
01:22:22.104 --> 01:22:23.811
Love takes thought and care,

1726
01:22:23.897 --> 01:22:26.765
and I'm glad that
all the plus columns lined up.

1727
01:22:26.859 --> 01:22:27.940
[laughter]

1728
01:22:28.026 --> 01:22:30.439
Kate, you're getting
one of the good ones.

1729
01:22:30.529 --> 01:22:32.441
[all] Aww...

1730
01:22:33.615 --> 01:22:36.278
Sorry, I said I wouldn't do this.
To Jared and Kate.

1731
01:22:38.537 --> 01:22:40.574
[guests] Cheers!

1732
01:22:45.544 --> 01:22:46.580
Oh!

1733
01:22:48.338 --> 01:22:49.920
I didn't mean to do that, sorry.

1734
01:22:50.257 --> 01:22:52.670
Um, as... as few...

1735
01:22:53.051 --> 01:22:54.713
Well, if any of you know,

1736
01:22:54.803 --> 01:22:57.295
I'm Jared's mother, Judge Meyers.

1737
01:22:58.182 --> 01:22:59.298
Or Sharon.

1738
01:23:00.184 --> 01:23:01.720
I just wanted to say,

1739
01:23:01.810 --> 01:23:04.348
I don't think that's what
Shakespeare had in mind

1740
01:23:04.438 --> 01:23:05.974
when he wrote those lines.

1741
01:23:06.940 --> 01:23:10.024
He was saying Cupid is blind.

1742
01:23:10.444 --> 01:23:12.811
He wasn't saying
that people should go

1743
01:23:12.905 --> 01:23:15.693
think themselves into love

1744
01:23:15.782 --> 01:23:18.240
and a system of pluses or minuses.

1745
01:23:18.327 --> 01:23:20.068
- Oh!
- [Sharon] But whatever.

1746
01:23:20.162 --> 01:23:23.121
Anyway, when I look at my son...

1747
01:23:23.749 --> 01:23:26.492
I am so proud of him because...

1748
01:23:27.211 --> 01:23:30.295
he has had the courage
to put himself out there,

1749
01:23:30.547 --> 01:23:33.255
and he's found someone
to make him happy.

1750
01:23:34.718 --> 01:23:36.334
That's inspiring.

1751
01:23:36.970 --> 01:23:39.633
Even for someone as old as me.

1752
01:23:39.723 --> 01:23:41.385
[laughter]

1753
01:23:42.100 --> 01:23:43.557
The truth is...

1754
01:23:44.561 --> 01:23:47.679
love is not blind,
and it's not a battlefield,

1755
01:23:47.773 --> 01:23:51.312
and it's not the sun or the moon
or everything we load onto it.

1756
01:23:52.778 --> 01:23:56.112
It's just a word
until someone gives it meaning.

1757
01:23:57.741 --> 01:24:00.484
And that's what the two of you
have found in each other.

1758
01:24:00.577 --> 01:24:02.819
In fact, all four of you.

1759
01:24:02.913 --> 01:24:04.996
And we all deserve that.

1760
01:24:05.374 --> 01:24:06.581
Well done.

1761
01:24:07.584 --> 01:24:08.574
[guests] Cheers!

1762
01:24:08.669 --> 01:24:10.205
[Tom] Kate and Jared.

1763
01:24:12.214 --> 01:24:14.922
[cell phone ringing]

1764
01:24:20.055 --> 01:24:21.421
[groans]

1765
01:24:22.349 --> 01:24:23.305
[groans] Hello?

1766
01:24:23.392 --> 01:24:25.133
[hotel operator] <i>Miss O'Donnell,
I'm calling to confirm</i>

1767
01:24:25.227 --> 01:24:27.310
<i>that Mr. Riley
has officially checked out.</i>

1768
01:24:27.729 --> 01:24:28.970
Thank you.

1769
01:24:31.942 --> 01:24:33.899
[doorbell ringing]

1770
01:24:33.986 --> 01:24:35.693
[door opening]

1771
01:24:37.531 --> 01:24:39.568
Hi, sweetie.

1772
01:24:39.658 --> 01:24:41.194
- [gasps]
- Hey.

1773
01:24:41.285 --> 01:24:44.153
What happened? We've been
trying to call all afternoon.

1774
01:24:44.788 --> 01:24:46.404
[Diane] What, you're still in a robe?

1775
01:24:46.498 --> 01:24:48.740
[Sharon] Carol's show starts in an hour.

1776
01:24:49.167 --> 01:24:51.204
I saw Arthur last night.

1777
01:24:51.295 --> 01:24:52.411
Oh, fun.

1778
01:24:52.504 --> 01:24:55.963
No! I broke up with him
once and for all.

1779
01:24:56.049 --> 01:24:57.210
[gasps]

1780
01:24:57.301 --> 01:24:58.633
- [Vivian] I did.
- What happened?

1781
01:24:58.719 --> 01:25:00.585
He told me he wanted to invite me

1782
01:25:00.679 --> 01:25:01.965
to move to New York with him,

1783
01:25:02.055 --> 01:25:04.092
but he realized
he didn't want to change me

1784
01:25:04.182 --> 01:25:06.344
because he loves me the way I am.

1785
01:25:06.643 --> 01:25:08.100
And he only wants to talk to me,

1786
01:25:08.186 --> 01:25:09.677
and he only wants to listen to me.

1787
01:25:09.771 --> 01:25:12.684
He told me I was his person.

1788
01:25:12.774 --> 01:25:15.312
[groans] I'm sorry. I mean,

1789
01:25:15.402 --> 01:25:17.564
I'm not actually following here.

1790
01:25:17.654 --> 01:25:19.065
No, me, neither.

1791
01:25:19.156 --> 01:25:21.899
You said that he loves you...
as you are?

1792
01:25:21.992 --> 01:25:23.483
[Carol]
He doesn't want to change you?

1793
01:25:23.577 --> 01:25:25.113
And he wanted to know your thoughts?

1794
01:25:25.203 --> 01:25:28.571
- So you broke up with him?
- Well, yeah, exactly! Duh.

1795
01:25:28.665 --> 01:25:30.031
Are you out of your mind?

1796
01:25:32.085 --> 01:25:33.667
Okay, where is he?

1797
01:25:33.754 --> 01:25:36.872
He checked out
and he's on his way to New York.

1798
01:25:36.965 --> 01:25:40.129
Okay. Okay.
Time to get dressed.

1799
01:25:40.218 --> 01:25:42.380
[Carol] Yup. That's it, Viv,
you're going after him.

1800
01:25:42.471 --> 01:25:45.259
- Get up, get up.
- [Vivian] No! Oh, my God.

1801
01:25:45.349 --> 01:25:46.715
What time is his flight?

1802
01:25:46.808 --> 01:25:49.016
- Huh?
- Never mind, I'll figure it out.

1803
01:25:49.102 --> 01:25:51.014
She has to put on something sexy.

1804
01:25:51.104 --> 01:25:52.936
Everything she owns is sexy!

1805
01:25:53.023 --> 01:25:55.766
I can't... Oh, God! It is so yucky,

1806
01:25:55.859 --> 01:25:57.225
and this is so needy!

1807
01:25:57.319 --> 01:25:59.231
Sharon, I am not desperate.

1808
01:25:59.321 --> 01:26:01.108
No, you are not. You are stupid.

1809
01:26:01.198 --> 01:26:04.407
No, I am not.
You just... You don't understand.

1810
01:26:04.493 --> 01:26:08.157
I know how this story ends,
and I do not like it.

1811
01:26:08.246 --> 01:26:10.533
If he has me, he's gonna get bored.

1812
01:26:10.624 --> 01:26:12.991
He hasn't seen me naked in 40 years!

1813
01:26:13.085 --> 01:26:14.667
I know. I'm sorry. Oh, my God...

1814
01:26:14.753 --> 01:26:17.621
I'm no fool! I know what happens.

1815
01:26:17.714 --> 01:26:19.296
He's gonna cheat on me

1816
01:26:19.383 --> 01:26:20.499
and leave me for a younger woman.

1817
01:26:20.592 --> 01:26:22.083
And then I'm gonna lose everything.

1818
01:26:22.177 --> 01:26:24.134
And it's just... it's not worth it!

1819
01:26:24.221 --> 01:26:26.338
- Okay, baby, there you go.
- It isn't worth it.

1820
01:26:26.431 --> 01:26:27.672
[shrieks]

1821
01:26:27.891 --> 01:26:29.757
I'm so sorry. I'm very sorry.

1822
01:26:29.851 --> 01:26:31.638
But it had to be done, all right?

1823
01:26:32.020 --> 01:26:33.556
[chuckles]

1824
01:26:33.647 --> 01:26:34.854
[laughter]

1825
01:26:35.315 --> 01:26:38.183
- It's okay.
- His flight leaves in an hour.

1826
01:26:38.276 --> 01:26:40.017
- God, are you sure?
- [Sharon] Yes.

1827
01:26:40.112 --> 01:26:41.978
Okay, earrings! Time to go.

1828
01:26:42.072 --> 01:26:44.109
- Do I look okay?
- Yes, you look great.

1829
01:26:44.199 --> 01:26:45.360
Oh, the girls.

1830
01:26:45.450 --> 01:26:47.692
- You want me to put those on?
- Yep. Go.

1831
01:26:47.786 --> 01:26:49.948
- Okay!
- Go, go, go, go!

1832
01:26:50.038 --> 01:26:51.370
[laughter]

1833
01:26:51.873 --> 01:26:54.115
I put a lipstick and compact in there.

1834
01:26:54.209 --> 01:26:56.201
Oh, that's so great!
Oh, thanks.

1835
01:26:56.294 --> 01:26:59.253
- Oh, my God, do I look okay?
- Yes! Yes.

1836
01:26:59.339 --> 01:27:00.580
[Diane cheers]

1837
01:27:00.674 --> 01:27:02.586
- [Sharon] Here we go.
- [Diane] Bye!

1838
01:27:02.676 --> 01:27:04.133
- Bye.
- [Vivian] Bye.

1839
01:27:04.553 --> 01:27:05.760
[doorbell]

1840
01:27:05.846 --> 01:27:07.337
[knocking]

1841
01:27:07.806 --> 01:27:09.422
My shoes.

1842
01:27:09.850 --> 01:27:11.682
Oh, and Carol, your show!

1843
01:27:11.768 --> 01:27:13.384
Oh, God, don't be ridiculous.

1844
01:27:13.478 --> 01:27:16.221
And Diane... you're leaving!

1845
01:27:16.314 --> 01:27:19.648
Oh, my God, you're leaving.
What am I gonna do?

1846
01:27:20.068 --> 01:27:21.309
Shoes!

1847
01:27:21.403 --> 01:27:23.690
Oh, God, thank you, guys.
I love you so much.

1848
01:27:28.702 --> 01:27:31.240
[shouts]
To the airport, Mario!

1849
01:27:31.329 --> 01:27:33.537
[Latin music playing]

1850
01:27:37.252 --> 01:27:39.585
[audience cheering]

1851
01:27:39.671 --> 01:27:41.162
Okay, that's scary.

1852
01:27:46.636 --> 01:27:49.174
[audience cheering]

1853
01:27:49.264 --> 01:27:51.426
You're gonna do great!
Gonna do great.

1854
01:27:51.516 --> 01:27:53.428
[audience whooping]

1855
01:27:55.854 --> 01:27:58.062
[audience cheering]

1856
01:28:01.526 --> 01:28:05.361
And that was Jed and Leyla
Sanderson performing!

1857
01:28:05.822 --> 01:28:08.439
Hard to believe
she's an anesthesiologist.

1858
01:28:09.201 --> 01:28:10.988
Arthur, it's Vivian. Call me back

1859
01:28:11.077 --> 01:28:12.443
before you board your plane.

1860
01:28:13.622 --> 01:28:15.534
Mario, are you using Waze?

1861
01:28:16.041 --> 01:28:18.328
[Mario] Yes, Miss O'Donnell,
but I don't think we're gonna make it.

1862
01:28:24.049 --> 01:28:26.086
And last but not least,

1863
01:28:26.176 --> 01:28:30.671
everyone's favorite chef
and our fearless organizer.

1864
01:28:30.972 --> 01:28:35.512
Dancing a solo will be...
Carol Colby!

1865
01:28:35.602 --> 01:28:37.685
[applause]

1866
01:28:37.771 --> 01:28:40.354
["I'd Do Anything for Love"
by Meat Loaf playing]

1867
01:28:40.440 --> 01:28:42.523
Wait. No, no, wait. Sorry.

1868
01:28:42.818 --> 01:28:44.309
That's not the right song.

1869
01:28:44.402 --> 01:28:46.268
It's supposed to be
"Red, Red Robin Goes Bob, Bob..."

1870
01:28:46.863 --> 01:28:49.355
Oh, shoot. Meat Loaf? Come on!

1871
01:28:49.449 --> 01:28:50.530
Aw, screw it.

1872
01:28:54.704 --> 01:28:58.197
Oh, my God, she's tap dancing
to Meat Loaf!

1873
01:28:58.291 --> 01:28:59.907
[Diane]
And she's pulling it off!

1874
01:29:02.629 --> 01:29:04.621
[feet tapping]

1875
01:29:17.561 --> 01:29:19.268
[Carol shrieks]

1876
01:29:38.623 --> 01:29:40.205
[cheering]

1877
01:29:41.418 --> 01:29:42.408
Bruce!

1878
01:29:42.502 --> 01:29:44.915
[cheering]

1879
01:29:54.472 --> 01:29:57.055
Five, six, seven, eight...

1880
01:30:21.917 --> 01:30:23.658
Oh, my God.

1881
01:30:26.671 --> 01:30:29.960
My, oh, my!
How about those Colbys?

1882
01:30:31.635 --> 01:30:33.968
A romantic way to end the show.

1883
01:30:36.806 --> 01:30:40.095
Oh God, I can't believe you're here.

1884
01:30:40.185 --> 01:30:43.223
I couldn't miss a chance
to dance with my girl.

1885
01:30:43.521 --> 01:30:45.513
- You were incredible.
- No, I wasn't.

1886
01:30:45.607 --> 01:30:47.690
None of our steps
go with Meat Loaf.

1887
01:30:48.193 --> 01:30:51.106
Who needs the steps?
We were dancing.

1888
01:30:57.869 --> 01:30:59.986
I'm sorry. Your cell phone
is poking me.

1889
01:31:00.080 --> 01:31:01.992
No, I didn't bring my cell phone.

1890
01:31:02.832 --> 01:31:05.449
- Oh.
- You want to go home now? What do you say?

1891
01:31:05.543 --> 01:31:07.034
- I say yes.
- Okay.

1892
01:31:21.142 --> 01:31:22.474
Arthur!

1893
01:31:24.270 --> 01:31:26.057
I thought you left.

1894
01:31:26.940 --> 01:31:28.021
I did.

1895
01:31:30.443 --> 01:31:33.356
I went to the airport to try to see you.

1896
01:31:37.075 --> 01:31:38.441
Why are you here?

1897
01:31:40.912 --> 01:31:42.528
I realized I...

1898
01:31:42.956 --> 01:31:44.743
forgot to give you back your penny.

1899
01:31:47.127 --> 01:31:48.618
Why did you go to the airport?

1900
01:31:50.505 --> 01:31:52.792
I realized I wanted my penny back.

1901
01:31:53.591 --> 01:31:57.551
See, I tried to live without it
for... for the past 40 years.

1902
01:31:58.638 --> 01:32:00.174
And I didn't like it.

1903
01:32:08.106 --> 01:32:09.642
Do you want to make a wish?

1904
01:32:11.026 --> 01:32:12.392
I do.

1905
01:32:16.865 --> 01:32:19.107
Oh, my God, you probably killed someone.

1906
01:32:21.327 --> 01:32:22.943
There's a subroof.

1907
01:32:41.514 --> 01:32:43.881
Nancy in my office,
she's in a book club,

1908
01:32:43.975 --> 01:32:45.557
and I thought
you might like to meet her.

1909
01:32:45.643 --> 01:32:47.885
Well, that's... that's very sweet.

1910
01:32:48.605 --> 01:32:50.096
Anyone else want
another piece of pizza?

1911
01:32:50.190 --> 01:32:51.146
I have one.

1912
01:32:52.108 --> 01:32:53.144
- Mom.
- What?

1913
01:32:53.234 --> 01:32:54.270
You're not hungry?

1914
01:32:55.236 --> 01:32:56.818
I guess not.

1915
01:32:56.905 --> 01:32:59.147
Well, I mean,
you're probably exhausted.

1916
01:32:59.240 --> 01:33:00.526
[scoffs]

1917
01:33:00.617 --> 01:33:03.280
It's really not okay
that you drove here all by yourself.

1918
01:33:03.369 --> 01:33:05.281
At your age, Mom,
you could have killed somebody.

1919
01:33:05.371 --> 01:33:06.487
I really don't think so.

1920
01:33:06.581 --> 01:33:08.698
And the fact that you
don't even realize that

1921
01:33:08.792 --> 01:33:09.908
is what is so scary.

1922
01:33:10.001 --> 01:33:11.162
Oh, Jesus! Will you just...

1923
01:33:11.252 --> 01:33:12.242
[groans]

1924
01:33:13.838 --> 01:33:15.704
Please stop, okay?

1925
01:33:16.883 --> 01:33:18.124
I mean, really!

1926
01:33:19.427 --> 01:33:20.543
Oh, my God.

1927
01:33:21.596 --> 01:33:22.552
Okay.

1928
01:33:26.184 --> 01:33:28.642
You know how proud I am
of both of you.

1929
01:33:31.314 --> 01:33:32.521
[sighs]

1930
01:33:33.525 --> 01:33:35.767
The greatest gift I think
a parent can give a child

1931
01:33:35.860 --> 01:33:37.146
is to lead by example,

1932
01:33:37.237 --> 01:33:39.399
and I don't think
I did a very good job.

1933
01:33:39.489 --> 01:33:40.696
But your father...

1934
01:33:40.782 --> 01:33:43.240
Oh, my goodness,
he was stable, wasn't he?

1935
01:33:43.326 --> 01:33:45.283
And smart and kind.

1936
01:33:45.370 --> 01:33:47.032
He was just a great dad.

1937
01:33:47.956 --> 01:33:50.323
Fine husband.
And we had a nice life.

1938
01:33:52.794 --> 01:33:56.333
But there's something...
I really have to say.

1939
01:34:01.553 --> 01:34:04.011
There's a man out there
who makes me feel things

1940
01:34:04.097 --> 01:34:05.929
that I didn't think were...

1941
01:34:06.516 --> 01:34:07.973
still possible.

1942
01:34:08.685 --> 01:34:10.301
You know what he does?
He makes me feel

1943
01:34:10.395 --> 01:34:13.012
curious and excited about the world.

1944
01:34:13.106 --> 01:34:16.349
And maybe things with us will go bust.

1945
01:34:16.442 --> 01:34:20.026
Maybe my feelings will be hurt,
but that's life.

1946
01:34:21.447 --> 01:34:23.860
And in spite of what
you both seem to think...

1947
01:34:24.784 --> 01:34:27.026
I'm not through living mine just yet.

1948
01:34:27.787 --> 01:34:29.369
I have things that I want to explore.

1949
01:34:29.455 --> 01:34:31.742
And guess what?
I think I've earned that right.

1950
01:34:31.833 --> 01:34:36.624
So it's time for all of this
to just stop, okay?

1951
01:34:37.922 --> 01:34:43.338
You both seem to have
very, very strong parenting instincts.

1952
01:34:43.428 --> 01:34:45.465
But do save it for your children

1953
01:34:45.555 --> 01:34:48.548
because your mother is doing just fine.

1954
01:34:50.602 --> 01:34:51.809
And...

1955
01:34:52.270 --> 01:34:54.136
I know I'm getting older.

1956
01:34:54.814 --> 01:34:57.306
But I'm still learning.

1957
01:34:57.817 --> 01:34:59.934
And one of the biggest
lessons I've learned

1958
01:35:00.028 --> 01:35:02.896
is not to be afraid to be happy.

1959
01:35:04.991 --> 01:35:06.573
I love you both.

1960
01:35:07.493 --> 01:35:09.530
But I'm not staying here anymore.

1961
01:35:11.247 --> 01:35:12.533
Mom...

1962
01:35:15.877 --> 01:35:17.584
Mom! Mom!

1963
01:35:20.298 --> 01:35:21.505
Have fun.

1964
01:35:26.387 --> 01:35:27.844
Love you.

1965
01:35:27.931 --> 01:35:29.513
- Love you, Mom.
- Love you.

1966
01:35:36.814 --> 01:35:39.181
- Drive safe!
- [Jill] Bye!

1967
01:35:39.275 --> 01:35:43.064
[pop music playing]

1968
01:36:25.947 --> 01:36:27.438
Can I come in?

1969
01:36:27.532 --> 01:36:28.739
No way.

1970
01:36:28.825 --> 01:36:30.407
- No way?
- No way.

1971
01:36:35.248 --> 01:36:38.207
- What's in the U-Haul?
- Just my overnight bag.

1972
01:36:52.598 --> 01:36:57.263
My inner goddess says,
"Most definitely yes."

1973
01:37:14.662 --> 01:37:16.654
[pop music playing]

1974
01:37:27.091 --> 01:37:29.504
Oh. Yeah, yeah, I see the arms.
